@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`

-- g2-conditions.l4: section 6 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems
-- Law 5785-2025, the conditions for granting a licence, and the Minister's power to change the Second Schedule.
--
-- IMPORTS.  prelude, daydate, il-interpretation-time, domain, and the group's own g2-validity and g2-second-schedule
-- (s 6(a)(4) is "in accordance with the Second Schedule", so it needs the Schedule engine).  No other group's module.
--
-- INPUTS this module takes, under the standard names of the survey's section (c): `the fee was paid in full` (IP11, group G8);
-- `the programme was approved by the Registrar` and `the foreign qualification was recognised` (IP5, group G4, ss 19(b) and
-- 19(c)); the Registrar's opinion of s 6(a)(3) (IP17); `the commencement day` (IP2, group G7); the Knesset committee's approval
-- of s 6(b).  Facts about the applicant are the `Applicant` and `Application` records of domain.l4.
-- No order under s 6(b) is in the sources (IP14): the Second Schedule as enacted is the only vintage modelled.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED.  s 6(a) is a duty: "the Registrar SHALL grant a licence to an applicant for whom all of (1) to (4) hold".
-- It is a regulative rule typed by the role that acts and by what is done: PARTY the Registrar MUST grant the licence sought,
-- with no WITHIN (the section states no period; inventing one would invent a period the Law does not enact).  Its conditions
-- (1) to (4) are booleans, one rule each.  s 6(b) is a power of the Minister (ruling 2 of the fleet lead: a power is encoded).
--
-- FORKS REGISTERED IN THIS MODULE (full text in FRAGMENT-G2.md section 2):
--   FC1  s 6(a) against regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations (group G8): s 6(a) says the Registrar SHALL grant; regulation 4 says
--        the Registrar shall NOT give a licence for which a fee was fixed unless it was paid in full.  TAKEN: payment of the fee
--        is a condition of the duty (the duty arises only where the fee was paid; s 59 empowers fees "for the grant of a
--        licence").  ALTERNATIVE: s 6(a) read alone, with regulation 4 a separate prohibition (the two then conflict
--        for an applicant who meets the conditions and has not paid).
--   FC2  s 6(a)(4) (trap T5 and the structure of the three limbs): TAKEN: (4) holds when one of (a), (b), (c) holds AND the
--        Second Schedule's requirement for the licence sought is met ("all in accordance with the Schedule").  On that reading
--        limb (c) is the Schedule's requirement itself, so the conjunction collapses to the Schedule; the limbs are encoded as
--        the Law writes them and the collapse is a finding (FRAGMENT section 6).  ALTERNATIVE: the Schedule asks nothing further
--        of an applicant who meets a limb ("in accordance with" read as no further condition).
--   FC3  The study programme and the foreign qualification (ss 19(b), 19(c)): TAKEN: the training or complementary studies the
--        Schedule requires count as completed when the applicant completed them in a programme the Registrar approved (s 19(b)),
--        or when the foreign qualification was recognised as meeting the training requirements (s 19(c)(1)).  ALTERNATIVE:
--        the programme's approval is not a condition of the applicant's completion (s 19(b) binds the programme, not the applicant).
--   FC4  s 2 "final certificate" (group G1, integration point IP5): TAKEN: every certificate the Schedule's column A names counts
--        as a final certificate (the Schedule itself names each one as a final certificate), the youth school certificate included.  ALTERNATIVE: the
--        youth school certificate does not count (s 2(1) asks for an examination the Division set, which is not stated of it).
--   FC7  The Division certificate that the course for the licence sought itself confers (grade N for a licence of grade N).  REPAIRED
--        2026-10-14 (defect D1, found by the independent test author and checked by the fleet lead): before then this module TOOK the
--        literal reading, in which that certificate is a column A entry of the ungraded rows (A3, B5(1), C6) and its holder is asked for
--        50, 50 or 200 hours more.  Now TAKEN: its holder has met item 1 and nothing further is asked of them.  The decision lives in the
--        engine of g2-second-schedule.l4 (fork FS10 there), so that `training required for the licence sought` and the duty here agree.
--        ALTERNATIVE, the literal reading: `s 6(a) under the reading` called with
--        `the reading with the Division certificate of the grade sought as an ordinary column A entry (FS10)`.  The three functions named
--        `(the certificate of the grade sought suffices)` below are kept for their callers and their assertions; since the repair they
--        give the same answers as the default.
--   FC5  The applicant's age (s 6(a)(1)): the Law gives no age; the word for "adult" in s 6(a)(1) is read as the applicant record's `of full age` flag.
--   FC6  s 6(b): TAKEN: a power that exists only with the committee's approval; without it no power arises (FULFILLED, nothing is
--        permitted).  The content of the order is not an input of this module: the Schedule as enacted is the only vintage.

§ `Section 6 — conditions for granting a licence`

@desc The acts of the Registrar and the Minister under section 6: granting the licence sought, and changing the Second Schedule by order
DECLARE `An act under section 6` IS ONE OF
    `grant the licence sought` HAS `the kind of licence` IS A `Licence kind`
    `change the Second Schedule by order`

-- The text of each limb of s 6 is copied by script from inputs/law.wiki, above the rule that encodes it.

-- src:85 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא בגיר;
@ref s 6(a)(1): the applicant is of full age (src:85)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application MEANS
    application's `the applicant`'s `of full age`

-- src:86 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא אזרח ישראלי או תושב ישראל;
@ref s 6(a)(2): the applicant is an Israeli citizen or an Israeli resident (src:86)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application MEANS
        application's `the applicant`'s `an Israeli citizen`
    OR  application's `the applicant`'s `an Israeli resident`

-- (3): "he was not convicted, and no indictment is pending against him, for a criminal offence which, by reason of its
-- nature, gravity or circumstances, in the opinion of the Registrar, makes him unfit to be a licensee".  The relative
-- clause qualifies the offence.  The Registrar's opinion is an input (a discretion, IP17); it matters only where the record
-- shows a conviction or a pending indictment.  The record's other fields (disciplinary offences, complaints) are not
-- "a criminal offence" and do not enter here.
-- src:87 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הוא לא הורשע ולא תלוי ועומד נגדו כתב אישום בעבירה פלילית שמפאת מהותה, חומרתה או נסיבותיה אין הוא ראוי, לדעת הרשם, להיות בעל רישיון;
@ref s 6(a)(3): no conviction or pending indictment for an offence that, in the Registrar's opinion, makes the applicant unfit (src:87)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` MEANS
    NOT (    (    application's `the applicant`'s `record of offences`'s `convicted of a criminal offence`
              OR  application's `the applicant`'s `record of offences`'s `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet`)
         AND `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`)

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (4) and its three limbs
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Section 6(a)(4) — one of three training routes, in accordance with the Second Schedule`

-- FC4.  "Final certificate" is defined in s 2 (group G1 owns the test, IP5).  This is the stand-in: every certificate that
-- column A of the Second Schedule names counts, because the Schedule itself names each one as a final certificate.
@ref s 2 "final certificate", read with s 6(a)(4)(a) (a stand-in for group G1's test, IP5)
GIVEN certificate IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 — the certificate counts as a final certificate` certificate MEANS
    CONSIDER certificate
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 1` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 2` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate of grade 3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Training Division certificate with no grade stated` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 3 study units` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Ministry of Education climate-control certificate of 5 study units` THEN TRUE

-- FC4, the alternative: the youth school certificate does not count.
@ref s 2 "final certificate", read with s 6(a)(4)(a) (a stand-in for group G1's test, IP5)
GIVEN certificate IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 (the youth school certificate not counted) — the certificate counts as a final certificate` certificate MEANS
    CONSIDER certificate
    WHEN `a certificate of the Training Division vocational school for youth` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `s 2 — the certificate counts as a final certificate` certificate

-- src:89 | {{ח:תתתת|(א)}} הוא בעל תעודת גמר;
@ref s 6(a)(4)(a): the applicant holds a final certificate (src:89)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` application MEANS
    any `s 2 — the certificate counts as a final certificate` (application's `the applicant`'s `certificates held`)

-- src:89 | {{ח:תתתת|(א)}} הוא בעל תעודת גמר;
@ref s 6(a)(4)(a), the youth school certificate not counted (src:89)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4)(a) (the youth school certificate not counted) — the applicant holds a final certificate` application MEANS
    any `s 2 (the youth school certificate not counted) — the certificate counts as a final certificate` (application's `the applicant`'s `certificates held`)

-- src:90 | {{ח:תתתת|(ב)}} הוא רשום במרשם ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים, בענף ובמדור קירור ומיזוג אוויר;
@ref s 6(a)(4)(b): the applicant is registered in the register of technicians and practical engineers, branch and section of refrigeration and air conditioning (src:90)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` application MEANS
        application's `the applicant`'s `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning`
    OR  application's `the applicant`'s `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning`

-- FC3.  The training and complementary studies that column B of the Second Schedule requires are completed when the
-- applicant completed them in a programme the Registrar approved (s 19(b)), or when the foreign qualification was
-- recognised as meeting the training requirements (s 19(c)(1)).
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, read with ss 19(b) and 19(c)
GIVEN `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        (`the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` AND `the programme was approved by the Registrar`)
    OR  `the foreign qualification was recognised`

-- FC3, the alternative: the programme's approval does not condition the applicant's completion.
@ref s 6(a) read with s 19(b) (fork FC3)
GIVEN `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4) (the programme's approval not a condition) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`
    OR  `the foreign qualification was recognised`

-- An entry of column B is met by an applicant: a course of training is met when the training requirement is met;
-- "the certificate itself" when the applicant holds that certificate; "no further requirement" always.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, read with ss 19(b) and 19(c)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the requirement` requirement `is met by` application `where the training requirement is met:` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `training of up to` ceiling certificate THEN `the training requirement is met`
    WHEN `column B: the certificate itself` certificate THEN elem certificate (application's `the applicant`'s `certificates held`)
    WHEN `column B: no further requirement` THEN TRUE

-- Whether the Schedule's requirement for the licence sought is met under a stated reading of the Schedule: some entry of column B of
-- some item that applies under that reading.  The reading is how the alternatives of FS1 to FS11 reach this module.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, read with ss 19(b) and 19(c)
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought under` `the reading` `is met for` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` `where the training requirement is met:` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
    any (GIVEN item YIELD
            any (GIVEN requirement YIELD `Second Schedule — the requirement` requirement `is met by` application `where the training requirement is met:` `the training requirement is met`)
                (item's `column B: any one of`))
        (`Second Schedule — the training required for the licence sought under` `the reading` `by` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day`)

-- Whether the Schedule's requirement for the licence sought is met: some entry of column B of some item that applies, on the reading taken.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, read with ss 19(b) and 19(c)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought is met` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought under` `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` `is met for` application `with commencement day` `the commencement day` `where the training requirement is met:` `the training requirement is met`

-- Whether the Schedule asks the applicant for training: no entry of column B that does not need training is met.
@ref s 6(a)(4) and the Second Schedule, read with ss 19(b) and 19(c)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` application `the commencement day` MEANS
    NOT `Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought is met` application `the commencement day` FALSE

-- src:91 | {{ח:תתתת|(ג)}} הוא סיים בהצלחה לימודי השלמה, אם נדרשים כאמור {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|בטור ב׳ בתוספת השנייה}}, בהתאם להכשרתו ולניסיונו הקודמים כאמור {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|בטור א׳ בתוספת האמורה}}.
@ref s 6(a)(4)(c): the applicant completed complementary studies, if column B of the Second Schedule requires them (src:91)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4)(c) — the applicant completed the complementary studies, if required` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
    IF   `Second Schedule — column B asks the applicant for training or complementary studies` application `the commencement day`
    THEN `the training requirement is met`
    ELSE TRUE

-- src:88 | {{ח:תתת|(4)}} מתקיים בו אחד התנאים שלהלן, והכול בהתאם לתנאים {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|שבתוספת השנייה}}:
@ref s 6(a)(4): one of (a), (b), (c) holds, all in accordance with the Second Schedule (src:88)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4) — one of the training routes holds, in accordance with the Second Schedule` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
        (    `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` application
         OR  `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` application
         OR  `s 6(a)(4)(c) — the applicant completed the complementary studies, if required` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met`)
    AND `Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought is met` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met`

-- FC2, the alternative: "all in accordance with the conditions of the Second Schedule" asks nothing further of an applicant who
-- meets one of the limbs.  Then the holder of a grade 1 final certificate, or a registered technician, qualifies by the limb alone
-- (the contradictions of FRAGMENT section 6: A3 against limb (a); Part A having no item for registrants against limb (b)).
@ref s 6(a)(4): one of (a), (b), (c) holds, the Schedule asking nothing further (src:88)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4) (the limbs alone) — one of the training routes holds` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
        `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` application
    OR  `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` application
    OR  `s 6(a)(4)(c) — the applicant completed the complementary studies, if required` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met`

-- FC7 (repaired 2026-10-14, defect D1).  The course of an item of the Part sought confers "a final certificate of grade N" for the licence
-- of grade N (A1(1), A2 and the rest of Part A confer grade 1; Part B grade 2; Part C grade 3).  Until the repair this module took the literal
-- reading, on which the holder of that very certificate was in the Division-certificate item of the same Part (A3, B5(1) or C6, whichever no
-- graded item names) and was asked for up to 50, 50 or 200 hours more: the applicant who completed C1's 720 hours and holds the grade 3
-- certificate it confers was asked for 200 more.  TAKEN NOW: the holder of the Division certificate of the grade sought has met item 1 and
-- nothing further is asked; the engine of g2-second-schedule decides it (fork FS10 there) and the chain `s 6(a)` ... `s 6(a)(4)` above follows
-- the engine.  The three functions below, named `(the certificate of the grade sought suffices)`, were the alternative while the literal
-- reading was the default; they are kept, with their assertions, and now give the same answers as the default chain.  The literal reading
-- is the alternative: `s 6(a) under the reading` below, called with the FS10 reading.
@ref s 6(a)(4)(a) read with column B of the Second Schedule (fork FC7)
GIVEN kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH A Certificate
`s 6(a)(4) (the certificate of the grade sought) — the Division certificate that the course for a licence of the kind confers` kind MEANS
    `Second Schedule — the Division certificate that item 1 of the Part leading to` kind

@ref s 6(a)(4)(a) read with column B of the Second Schedule: the holder of the final certificate the course for the licence sought confers (src:89)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the training requirement is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a)(4) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — one of the training routes holds` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met` MEANS
        elem (`s 6(a)(4) (the certificate of the grade sought) — the Division certificate that the course for a licence of the kind confers` (application's `the kind of licence sought`))
             (application's `the applicant`'s `certificates held`)
    OR  `s 6(a)(4) — one of the training routes holds, in accordance with the Second Schedule` application `the commencement day` `the training requirement is met`

@ref s 6(a)(4)(a) read with column B of the Second Schedule (fork FC7)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application
    AND `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`
    AND `s 6(a)(4) (the certificate of the grade sought suffices) — one of the training routes holds` application `the commencement day`
            (`s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met`
                `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`
                `the programme was approved by the Registrar`
                `the foreign qualification was recognised`)

-- s 6(a) under a stated reading of the Second Schedule: the conditions (1) to (4) with the engine called with that reading throughout.
-- This is how every alternative of FS1 to FS11 reaches the conditions as a whole; with `the reading of the Second Schedule taken` it
-- agrees with `s 6(a) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold`, and with the FS10 reading it is the literal reading of FC7.
@ref s 6(a)(1) to (4) read with the Second Schedule and ss 19(b) and 19(c), under a stated reading (forks FS1 to FS11, FC7)
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of the Second Schedule`
      application IS AN Application
      day IS A DATE
      opinion IS A BOOLEAN
      completed IS A BOOLEAN
      approved IS A BOOLEAN
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) under the reading` reading `— the conditions (1) to (4) all hold for` application `with commencement day` day `, opinion` opinion `, completion` completed `, approval` approved `and recognition` recognised MEANS
        `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application
    AND `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application opinion
    AND (    `s 6(a)(4)(a) — the applicant holds a final certificate` application
         OR  `s 6(a)(4)(b) — the applicant is registered as a technician or practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` application
         OR  (IF   `Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought under` reading `is met for` application `with commencement day` day `where the training requirement is met:` FALSE
              THEN trainingMet
              ELSE TRUE))
    AND `Second Schedule — the requirement for the licence sought under` reading `is met for` application `with commencement day` day `where the training requirement is met:` trainingMet
    WHERE
        trainingMet MEANS
            `s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met` completed approved recognised

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (a): the duty
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Section 6(a) — the Registrar's duty to grant`

-- src:84 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הרשם ייתן רישיון למבקש שמתקיימים לגביו כל אלה:
@ref s 6(a): the conditions (1) to (4) all hold (src:84)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application
    AND `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`
    AND `s 6(a)(4) — one of the training routes holds, in accordance with the Second Schedule` application `the commencement day`
            (`s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met`
                `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`
                `the programme was approved by the Registrar`
                `the foreign qualification was recognised`)

-- FC3, the alternative taken through every limb: the programme's approval is not a condition.
@ref s 6(a) read with s 19(b) (fork FC3)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) (the programme's approval not a condition) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application
    AND `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`
    AND `s 6(a)(4) — one of the training routes holds, in accordance with the Second Schedule` application `the commencement day`
            (`s 6(a)(4) (the programme's approval not a condition) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met`
                `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`
                `the foreign qualification was recognised`)

-- FC2, the alternative taken through all of s 6(a): the limbs of (4) alone.
@ref s 6(a)(4) (fork FC2)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) (the limbs of (4) alone) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
        `s 6(a)(1) — the applicant is of full age` application
    AND `s 6(a)(2) — the applicant is an Israeli citizen or resident` application
    AND `s 6(a)(3) — no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment` application `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`
    AND `s 6(a)(4) (the limbs alone) — one of the training routes holds` application `the commencement day`
            (`s 6(a)(4) with ss 19(b) and 19(c) — the training requirement of the Second Schedule is met`
                `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed`
                `the programme was approved by the Registrar`
                `the foreign qualification was recognised`)

-- The duty.  FC1: the fee is a condition of the duty (regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations, group G8).  The act is typed by
-- the role that acts (PARTY the Registrar) and by what is done (grant the licence sought).  No WITHIN: s 6(a) fixes none.
-- src:84 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הרשם ייתן רישיון למבקש שמתקיימים לגביו כל אלה:
@ref s 6(a): the Registrar shall grant a licence to an applicant who meets all of (1) to (4) (src:84)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 6`
`s 6(a) — the Registrar must grant the licence` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` `the fee was paid in full` MEANS
    IF       `s 6(a) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised`
         AND `the fee was paid in full`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `grant the licence sought` (application's `the kind of licence sought`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- FC1, the alternative: s 6(a) read alone.  Regulation 4 is then a separate prohibition (group G8), and the Registrar is under
-- both a duty and a prohibition for an applicant who meets the conditions and has not paid.
@ref s 6(a): the Registrar shall grant a licence to an applicant who meets all of (1) to (4), read without regulation 4 (src:84)
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 6`
`s 6(a) (read without regulation 4) — the Registrar must grant the licence` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` MEANS
    IF   `s 6(a) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `grant the licence sought` (application's `the kind of licence sought`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 6(a), as an answer for a wizard: whether the Registrar is bound to grant the licence (src:84)
@export Whether the Registrar must grant the licence sought: the conditions of s 6(a)(1) to (4) all hold (full age; citizen or resident; no disqualifying conviction or pending indictment in the Registrar's opinion; one of the three training routes in accordance with the Second Schedule) and the fee was paid in full
GIVEN application IS AN Application @desc The licence application: the applicant and what they hold, the kind of licence sought, the day of the application
      `the commencement day` IS A DATE @desc The commencement day of the Law (s 63(a)(1)), from which the three-year note on the Schedule's experience items runs
      `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar is of the opinion that a criminal offence the applicant was convicted of, or is charged with and awaits judgment on, makes the applicant unfit by its nature, gravity or circumstances; read only where the record shows a conviction or a pending indictment
      `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant completed the training or complementary studies that column B of the Second Schedule requires of them
      `the programme was approved by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the study programme the applicant completed had the Registrar's consent (s 19(b))
      `the foreign qualification was recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar recognised the applicant's foreign certificate, title or training as meeting the training requirements (s 19(c))
      `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the applicant paid the fee for the licence in full (regulation 4 of the Fees Regulations)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar must grant the licence` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised` `the fee was paid in full` MEANS
        `s 6(a) — the conditions (1) to (4) all hold` application `the commencement day` `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` `the training or complementary studies that the Second Schedule requires were completed` `the programme was approved by the Registrar` `the foreign qualification was recognised`
    AND `the fee was paid in full`

-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (b): the Minister's power to change the Second Schedule
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Section 6(b) — the Minister's power to change the Second Schedule`

-- FC6.  A power of the Minister, with the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee's approval as its procedural
-- precondition (ruling 2: a power is encoded, not left inert).  The CONTENT of an order is not modelled: the Second Schedule
-- as enacted is the only vintage (IP14).  Without the approval no power arises: nothing is permitted.
-- src:92 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 2|התוספת השנייה}}.
@ref s 6(b): the Minister, with the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee, may change the Second Schedule by order (src:92)
GIVEN `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 6`
`s 6(b) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
    IF   `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister` MAY `change the Second Schedule by order`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- FC6, the alternative: the same power read as one that is withheld without the approval, so that an order made without it is a
-- breach of a prohibition and not merely the absence of a power.
@ref s 6(b): the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order only with the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee's approval (src:92)
GIVEN `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 6`
`s 6(b) (an order without the approval is forbidden) — the Minister may change the Second Schedule by order` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
    IF   `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister` MAY `change the Second Schedule by order`
    ELSE PARTY `the Minister`
         SHANT `change the Second Schedule by order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 6(b): the Second Schedule was changed by order without the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee"
